# (#218) In a MODULE-observed program (the observer reads `z` at module
# scope; the function itself observes nothing) the module numeric has no C
# static -- reads go through the env -- and the pair's fallback read is
# that env read. Measured on the pin: the function's call-local writes do
# not observe the module slot (report/stable answer exactly as in the
# control program without the writes), and the module value stays 1.
z is 1.0
define u() as:
    z is 0.25
    z is 0.5
    return prev of z
print of (u of [])
print of z
print of (report of z)
print of (stable of z)
z is 3.0
z is 3.0
print of (u of [])
print of z
print of (report of z)
print of (stable of z)
